cards.text:
{red|**Reflect on where you are in the balance between memory and life.**

Are you holding on so tightly to the past that you cannot move forward?}

{red|Are you rushing away from the past so quickly that you are not honoring their memory?}

{red|What does healthy balance look like for you?}

{red|What would your spouse want for you?}{red| Would they want you frozen in grief?}{red| Would they want you to forget them?}{red| Or would they want you to remember them and live fully?}

{red|What is one way you could honor their memory this week?}

{red|What is one way you could take a step toward new life this week?}

{red|**Think about what rituals or practices might help you honor your spouse's memory.**

What daily or regular practice might work for you?}{red| Something small that keeps them present?}

{red|How do you want to mark their birthday?}{red| What would feel meaningful?}

{red|How do you want to mark your anniversary?}{red| What honors the marriage?}

{red|How do you want to mark the death anniversary?}{red| What helps you grieve and remember?}

{red|Are there other occasions or practices that feel right for you?}

**You do not need many rituals.** You need ones that fit you, that feel meaningful, that you will actually do.

{red|**Think about your spouse's belongings and what feels right.**

Are you ready to address their things?}{red| If not, that is okay. When might you be ready?}

{red|If you are ready, what items are most meaningful to keep?}{red| What holds real significance?}

{red|What items might be meaningful to pass on to family or friends?}

{red|What could be donated to help others?}

{red|What can be released without guilt?}

**You do not have to decide everything now.** But beginning to think about it can help when the time comes.

{red|**Think about the stories that deserve to be told and preserved.**

What stories about your spouse do only you know?}

{red|What stories should your children or grandchildren hear?}

{red|What stories capture who they really were, their character, their humor, their love?}

{red|Have you asked others for their stories about your spouse?}{red| What might you learn?}

{red|How might you preserve these stories?}{red| Writing, recording, gathering?}

{red|When considering legacy projects, ask: What would they want?}

{red|What did they care about most?}{red| What causes, people, or values mattered to them?}

{red|What would make them proud?}{red| If they could see how you honor their memory, what would bring them joy?}

{red|What would they encourage you to do?}{red| Not out of obligation, but out of love?}

{red|**Some people feel pressure to create elaborate memorials.** But often, the simplest tributes are most meaningful. A tree planted in their favorite place. Regular support for a cause they loved. Living out the values they taught.

Ask yourself: Is this for them or for me?} The best legacy projects honor who they actually were, not a version of them you are constructing.

**"Let your light shine before others, that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven" ({red|Matthew 5:16|Let your light shine before others, that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven}).** Let your spouse's light continue to shine through the good deeds done in their memory.

{red|**Consider what legacy projects might honor your spouse.**

What causes or organizations did they care about?}

{red|What values did they hold that you could continue to live out?}

{red|What unfinished projects or dreams might be worth continuing?}

{red|What would be meaningful to them?}{red| What would make them proud?}

{red|What is realistic for you to take on?}{red| Not what you should do, but what you actually can and want to do?}

**You do not have to do everything.** One meaningful action is enough.

{red|**Think about how you can help your children keep their parent's memory.**

What stories should they hear?}{red| What do they need to know about their parent?}

{red|What concrete items might help younger children?}{red| Photos, belongings, tangible connections?}

{red|Do your children have permission to talk about their parent?}{red| Have you explicitly invited their memory?}

{red|What questions might they have that you could answer?}

{red|What memory-keeping activities could you do together?}{red| Scrapbooks, visits to meaningful places, watching old videos?}

{red|How might memory keeping look different for children of different ages?}

{red|**Reflect on making space for new memories and experiences.**

What new experiences have you allowed yourself?}{red| How did they feel?}

{red|What new experiences are you resisting?}{red| Why?}

{red|What would you try if guilt were not a factor?}

{red|How do you think your spouse would feel about you having new experiences?}

{red|What new first might you be ready for?}{red| A trip, a hobby, a connection?}

{red|What guilt do you need to release to allow new joy into your life?}

{red|**Reflect on any experiences of your spouse's presence.**

Have you sensed their presence?}{red| In what ways?}

{red|Have you had vivid dreams of them?}{red| What were they like?}

{red|Have there been coincidences that felt like signs?}{red| Moments that seemed meaningful?}

{red|How have these experiences affected you?}{red| Comforted you, unsettled you, both?}

{red|How do you interpret these experiences?}{red| What do you make of them?}

{red|If you have not had such experiences, how do you feel about that?}

{red|**Reflect on how to integrate your spouse into your ongoing life.**

What parts of them do you carry in who you are?}{red| Character, values, perspectives they gave you?}

{red|How do they continue to influence your decisions, your relationships, your life?}

{red|What would they want you to carry forward?}{red| What hopes did they have for you?}

{red|How can honoring their memory and living fully coexist?}

{red|What does it look like for them to remain part of your story as you continue living it?}

{red|**Reflect on the path forward from here.**

How will you honor your spouse's memory in the months and years ahead?}

{red|How will you allow yourself to continue living, experiencing new things, finding joy?}

{red|What balance feels right for you between memory and new life?}

{red|What would your spouse want for your future?}

{red|What do you hope for yourself?}
